---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Note from '@/components/Note.astro';
import { allPapers, igNobelCount } from '@/lib/papers';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About: how we pick the funniest research papers"
  description="Little Miss Research collects real, published research papers that are hilarious, and explains them in plain English. Here's how we choose them."
>
  <div class="container--narrow">
    <header class="page-header">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About' }]} />
      
      <h1 class="headline">About this little paper</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose about">
      <p class="lede">
        Science is mostly careful, slow, brilliant work. And sometimes it’s a physicist wondering whether a cat is a liquid.
        This is a love letter to those papers, and to the curious people who write them.
      </p>

      <h2>What’s in here?</h2>
      <p>
        {allPapers.length} real research papers (and a couple of official internet standards) that made us laugh, explained
        in normal-person language. {igNobelCount} of them won an <a href="https://improbable.com/ig/">Ig Nobel Prize</a>,
        the award for research that “makes people laugh, then think”.
      </p>

      <h2>How we pick</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>It has to be real.</strong> Published in a journal, presented at a conference or issued as an official standard. No made-up papers, ever.</li>
        <li><strong>It has to be funny.</strong> Funny title, funny question, funny method, or a funny result. Bonus points for all four.</li>
        <li><strong>We laugh with researchers.</strong> Never at anyone. Science is better with a giggle.</li>
        <li><strong>It should teach you something.</strong> Most of these papers are secretly very clever. We try to explain why.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>The silliness scale</h2>
      <p>Every paper gets a rating from 1 (mildly amusing) to 5 (pure delight). This scale is not peer-reviewed. It runs entirely on vibes.</p>

      <h2>Can I read the original papers?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes, please do! Every page has a “find the original paper” button. Our summaries are simplified on purpose, so
        if you’re citing something, cite the real paper and not us.
      </p>

      <h2>Spotted a mistake?</h2>
      <p>
        We try very hard to get the facts right, but we’re only human (Chester the cat was unavailable for review). If
        something’s off, let us know and we’ll fix it.
      </p>
      <Note tilt="right">thank you for being a nerd with us ♡</Note>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
  }
  .about ol {
    padding-inline-start: 1.2em;
  }
  .about li + li {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
